@moduledoc """
What happens to a dropped file once it is scanned clean: the module named by
`config <%= inspect(@app) %>, <%= inspect(@file_drop) %>, handler: …` (`<%= inspect(@file_drop) %>.Handlers.Keep`,
which only keeps it, until the application has its own).

`handle/2` runs in the upload's `:ingest` job, outside any transaction, and
returns:

  * `{:ok, summary}` - done; the map is stored as the upload's `result` and
    shown on the page,
  * `{:reject, message}` - this file will never work (wrong format, nothing in
    it); the upload is `:failed` with `message`, and is not retried,
  * `{:error, reason}` - try again later; after the last attempt the upload is
    `:failed`.

The same bytes are never handed over twice for one organization, but a retry
hands over the same upload again: be idempotent.

`hints/1`, when defined, is what the page offers in its "What is this?" select;
the chosen value is the upload's `hint`.
"""

@callback handle(upload :: <%= inspect(@file_drop) %>.Upload.t(), body :: binary()) ::
            {:ok, map()} | {:reject, String.t()} | {:error, term()}

@callback hints(organization :: map()) :: [{label :: String.t(), value :: String.t()}]

@optional_callbacks hints: 1
